# Who reviews what. GitHub requests a review from the owners of every file a pull request touches,
# and branch protection on the release branch requires it. The last matching line wins.
#
# The owner is one account for now; when the repository moves to an organisation this becomes the
# dev team (@<org>/cordon-dev), here and nowhere else.

# Everything, by default.
*                                           @Threx-code

# What the scan's own integrity rests on: the guard manifest and every file it pins.
/.cordon-guard.sha256                       @Threx-code
/cordon-history-baseline.json               @Threx-code
/.github/workflows/                         @Threx-code

# The package's arrangement and the test that holds it (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Package layout").
/tests/unit/repository/test_package_layout.py   @Threx-code
/tests/unit/package_layout.json             @Threx-code

# What decides which code loads: the entry points, and the registries the engine reaches adapters by.
/pyproject.toml                             @Threx-code
/src/cordon_scanner/engine/registry.py      @Threx-code

# This file.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                         @Threx-code
